   "fen": "4r2k/p1pb1pR1/2p4B/3pr3/8/2PB4/P1P2PPP/R5K1 w - - 1 20",
   "line": [
    "Kh8"
   ],
   "spoken": "Making luft doesn't have to be the reflexive rook-pawn move — here a different pawn push serves two purposes at once, both parrying an annoying rook lunge and preparing to anchor a piece. In the endgame especially, if another luft move accomplishes something extra, don't be afraid to play it.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
