   "spoken": "A formalised idea worth carrying — the diminishing-returns theory. Winning the first piece is enormous, taking the position from equal to winning; a second piece adds less; and each additional pawn after that adds less still. So grab free pawns, yes, but never damage your position to win one more.",
   "kind": "plan",
   "reanchor": true
  },
